<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vytenis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1316</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vytenis was grand duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> from about 1295 to 1316. He waged long wars against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, allied with the city of Riga against the Livonian Order and extended Lithuanian influence over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-ruthenia">Black Ruthenia</a>. He was succeeded by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gediminas">Gediminas</a>, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gediminids">Gediminid dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vytenis.jpg" alt="Vytenis" width="320" height="317" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aleksander Gwagnin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vytenis_(99259232).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
